WEBVTT

00:06.050 --> 00:08.400
Wow, this is impressive!

00:08.400 --> 00:10.740
Feels like we're at a party for the pirate king.

00:11.680 --> 00:14.410
You think it's okay to 
help ourselves like this?

00:14.410 --> 00:17.040
Well, what good are leftovers gonna do?

00:17.040 --> 00:20.290
Don't overdo it now, Charlotte.

00:20.290 --> 00:21.750
Same to you, Aurora-chan.

00:24.620 --> 00:27.890
Should we really be splurging like this?

00:27.890 --> 00:29.680
Oh, of course.

00:29.680 --> 00:32.560
As long as you're willing to 
humor me with one thing.

00:33.930 --> 00:38.310
If you'd all pay attention to the stage!

00:38.310 --> 00:39.510
That voice...

00:39.790 --> 00:41.420
Ready, and...

00:40.680 --> 00:43.520
<b>Yuzaki Nasa
& Tsukasa

Surprise Reception</b>

00:40.680 --> 00:43.520
<b>Yuzaki Nasa
& Tsukasa

Surprise Reception</b>

00:45.560 --> 00:49.900
<b>Episode 11      On a Moonlit Night</b>

00:46.800 --> 00:48.100
Kaname?

00:51.030 --> 00:52.340
Nakiri-san?

00:53.320 --> 00:56.190
This was a lot of work, you know.

00:58.280 --> 01:02.290
<b>The Romantic History
of the Yuzakis</b>

00:58.280 --> 01:02.290
<b>The Romantic History
of the Yuzakis</b>

00:58.280 --> 01:03.040
Two years ago, on a snowy night, 
our lovers had their fateful meeting!

01:03.400 --> 01:07.920
"Wow, what a cutie pie! 
I can't wait to smooch her!"

01:08.230 --> 01:09.270
Whoa, hang on!

01:09.270 --> 01:11.500
What exactly is this montage?!

01:11.500 --> 01:14.930
Those were Yuzaki Nasa's thoughts 
after his first glimpse of Tsukassan.

01:14.930 --> 01:17.290
"I have to marry her!"

01:17.290 --> 01:18.820
And yet!

01:19.680 --> 01:24.140
Senpai ended up smooching a truck before 
he got a chance with his future wife!

01:25.020 --> 01:28.400
But it was then that the 
gears of fate began to spin!

01:28.960 --> 01:31.500
He was saved by the dashing Tsukassan!

01:31.500 --> 01:34.030
This narration and these 
pictures don't match at all!

01:34.030 --> 01:36.490
<b>Instant Death</b>

01:34.980 --> 01:38.090
If it hadn't been for her, 
he would've died in an instant.

01:38.090 --> 01:41.840
But right after that, Tsukassan disappeared!

01:41.840 --> 01:43.520
"I want to see her again!"

01:43.520 --> 01:47.040
This was how Senpai's 
dramatic two years began.

01:47.320 --> 01:52.160
For two years, day in and day 
out, he continued his search.

01:52.160 --> 01:56.530
Desperate to see her again, despite 
no guarantee that he ever could!

01:56.530 --> 01:58.940
In the pouring rain, in the freezing snow,

01:58.940 --> 02:04.430
through exhaustion and illness, 
it was all to see Tsukassan again!

02:04.430 --> 02:07.690
<b>T{*\c&HE0E096&}h{*\c&HE0DD92&}e {*\c&HE2D789&}D{*\c&HE2D484&}a{*\c&HE3D180&}y {*\c&HE4CB77&}o{*\c&HE5C872&}f {*\c&HE6C269&}H{*\c&HE7BF64&}i{*\c&HE8BC60&}s {*\c&HE9B757&}1{*\c&HEAB452&}8{*\c&HEAB14E&}t{*\c&HEBAE49&}h {*\c&HECA840&}B{*\c&HEDA53B&}i{*\c&HEEA237&}r{*\c&HEE9F32&}t{*\c&HEF9C2E&}h{*\c&HF09929&}d{*\c&HF09625&}ay</b>

02:04.690 --> 02:06.990
Then, on his 18th birthday,

02:06.990 --> 02:09.680
the two were reunited at long last!

02:07.690 --> 02:09.440
<b>A Fated Reunion</b>

02:10.440 --> 02:13.440
Leading to their marriage, 
which brings us to today.

02:14.850 --> 02:16.490
Uh...

02:16.490 --> 02:19.320
Bravo!

02:19.710 --> 02:23.330
Congratulations!

02:23.330 --> 02:25.700
What exactly is this, Kaname?!

02:26.160 --> 02:30.960
Well, what else do you do 
at a wedding reception?

02:30.960 --> 02:32.490
R-Reception?

02:32.490 --> 02:33.840
Yep.

02:34.270 --> 02:37.260
Tokiko-san was dead set on making it happen,

02:37.260 --> 02:40.710
and we got Nakiri-san's help 
to make sure it was a surprise.

02:40.710 --> 02:43.260
I planned the whole thing!

02:43.260 --> 02:46.100
I've never heard of a 
surprise reception before!

02:46.400 --> 02:48.180
What's the problem?

02:48.190 --> 02:52.380
You've got all these people 
who like you in one place.

02:52.380 --> 02:55.320
It'd be a waste not to 
embarrass you a little.

02:55.610 --> 02:57.680
Or did you think I was 
feeding you all for free?

02:57.680 --> 02:59.070
What sense does that make?!

02:59.360 --> 03:03.200
Be honest. That little montage 
was pretty touching, wasn't it?

03:04.560 --> 03:05.490
Well...

03:06.420 --> 03:07.950
That's great to hear.

03:07.950 --> 03:10.860
Makes the work we put into it worthwhile.

03:11.660 --> 03:14.380
Did that girl put the whole montage together?

03:14.380 --> 03:16.780
She must really like her senpai.

03:16.780 --> 03:18.590
What a sweetie!

03:18.920 --> 03:22.600
Now, I'd like to invite our 
stars up to the stage!

03:23.440 --> 03:25.000
Wait, what?! Why?!

03:25.000 --> 03:28.210
Well, this is literally all about you two.

03:28.210 --> 03:29.850
We never asked for that!

03:30.370 --> 03:34.690
Still, Kaname-chan and the others did 
put in a lot of effort for our sake.

03:35.590 --> 03:36.650
Damn...

03:36.650 --> 03:38.540
That's such a Kaname move!

03:38.540 --> 03:41.240
She's been busy with finals and housework, too.

03:41.630 --> 03:45.010
Kaname really tackles her goals head-on.

03:45.010 --> 03:46.850
If you'd just step this way...

03:49.280 --> 03:52.750
Fine! You just want me up there, right?!

03:54.560 --> 03:56.710
Now that they've joined me on stage,

03:56.710 --> 04:02.260
how about a big round of applause for our 
bride and groom, Yuzaki Nasa and Tsukasa?

04:02.550 --> 04:05.720
Now that we're on stage, 
what exactly is the plan?

04:05.720 --> 04:12.000
Well, it's a reception, so of course we're 
going to have a few words from our newlyweds!

04:11.520 --> 04:13.270
<b>Surprise Reception
~ Speech of Love ~</b>

04:11.520 --> 04:13.270
<b>Surprise Reception
~ Speech of Love ~</b>

04:13.270 --> 04:14.520
Huh?

04:14.520 --> 04:15.800
Words?

04:15.800 --> 04:18.020
You can't expect us to 
just improvise a speech!

04:18.290 --> 04:22.490
It's fine! It doesn't need 
to be formal or anything.

04:22.490 --> 04:24.360
A casual one isn't much easier!

04:24.360 --> 04:26.140
If you insist...

04:26.140 --> 04:27.400
You do it, then, Senpai!

04:28.240 --> 04:30.900
This is a perfect chance for you to nail it.

04:30.900 --> 04:32.660
What?! Me?!

04:36.140 --> 04:37.130
Got it.

04:37.130 --> 04:38.290
Really?!

04:38.770 --> 04:40.430
Here's your mic.

04:43.320 --> 04:45.300
Well, uh...

04:45.600 --> 04:48.830
Th-Thank you all for joining us 
on this auspicious occasion.

04:48.830 --> 04:50.150
Er...

04:50.150 --> 04:53.430
I wonder why he gets so 
nervous when he's on the mic.

04:53.700 --> 04:57.970
Um... I'm not sure what's 
the best way to put this,

04:58.400 --> 05:00.970
but I like Tsukasa-chan...

05:00.970 --> 05:04.450
Like her a lot. No, I love her.

05:04.980 --> 05:09.980
And if I start describing why, 
I could go on all night...

05:10.450 --> 05:16.210
But it's my intention to cherish 
those feelings as we start our new life,

05:16.760 --> 05:23.960
on a journey together, with the support 
of everyone who's gathered here tonight.

05:24.440 --> 05:28.000
Thank you very much for coming.

05:28.470 --> 05:30.970
Congratulations!

05:30.970 --> 05:32.470
Good one, good one!

05:35.470 --> 05:38.490
Your hubby's pretty smooth, huh, Tsukassan?

05:38.490 --> 05:39.860
Oh, pipe down!

05:40.200 --> 05:43.030
And now for another surprise!

05:44.590 --> 05:46.610
It wouldn't be a reception without this!

05:47.060 --> 05:49.500
They say the first thing 
spouses do together...

05:49.500 --> 05:51.620
is cut the cake!

05:52.620 --> 05:54.070
That's a huge cake!

05:54.070 --> 05:57.750
She hauled that thing up a 
mountain! You rock, Kaname!

05:58.110 --> 06:03.630
Yes, if you only knew how cautious 
I had to be in bringing it to you all.

06:04.440 --> 06:07.210
Hey, so we just cut it with this knife?

06:07.210 --> 06:08.320
Whoa, one sec!

06:08.320 --> 06:09.390
Before we begin...

06:14.150 --> 06:15.440
A veil?

06:15.440 --> 06:20.150
We can save the wedding dress 
for your actual wedding,

06:20.420 --> 06:24.530
but you've got to at least 
look the part a little.

06:29.980 --> 06:31.220
It's so cute!

06:31.220 --> 06:33.660
Amazing how one item can make 
her look more like a bride.

06:33.910 --> 06:36.850
Unbelievable... What were they thinking?

06:36.850 --> 06:40.330
But you look really beautiful.

06:41.760 --> 06:43.590
Th-Thank you.

06:45.580 --> 06:48.510
Now, you may cut the cake!

06:50.690 --> 06:53.100
Congratulations!

06:54.540 --> 06:55.830
Looks good!

06:55.830 --> 06:58.320
Congratulations!

07:08.560 --> 07:11.360
<i>Why do people get married?</i>

07:12.320 --> 07:15.920
<i>It's believed that in ancient Egypt,
 people would put rings—</i>

07:15.920 --> 07:20.370
<i>symbols of eternity—on the left ring finger
 during wedding ceremonies.</i>

07:20.790 --> 07:23.330
<i>Marriage is so ingrained in human history,</i>

07:23.330 --> 07:26.010
<i>it's hard to trace its origin.</i>

07:26.720 --> 07:30.380
<i>But the question remains: 
why do people get married?</i>

07:34.480 --> 07:36.390
That's the summer triangle.

07:36.640 --> 07:41.110
Clockwise from the top, 
you can see Vega, Altair, and Deneb.

07:41.110 --> 07:42.960
Vega is in the Lyra constellation,

07:42.960 --> 07:44.270
and Altair is in Aquila.

07:44.790 --> 07:47.630
You can see the Milky Way 
in the middle there,

07:47.630 --> 07:49.780
which means those two stars,
 in Japanese folklore,

07:50.120 --> 07:52.030
are Orihime and Hikoboshi.

07:52.030 --> 07:54.000
You really know your stuff!

07:54.000 --> 07:57.030
They did name me Nasa, 
with the kanji for "starry sky."

07:57.400 --> 08:00.110
The stars really are beautiful, though.

08:00.110 --> 08:03.040
This must be what they mean when they
say it looks like it'll start raining stars.

08:03.360 --> 08:05.950
I can't tell them apart at all, though.

08:05.950 --> 08:09.480
Yeah, they all look the same to me.

08:10.640 --> 08:13.050
Say, what's that big red one?

08:14.200 --> 08:16.400
That'd be Antares.

08:16.400 --> 08:18.290
It's at the core of the 
Scorpius constellation,

08:18.290 --> 08:21.260
and it's around 720 times 
bigger than our sun.

08:22.030 --> 08:24.440
That one is Brachium, part of Libra.

08:24.440 --> 08:29.690
And above it is the double 
star system, Zubenelgenubi.

08:29.960 --> 08:32.720
I'm genuinely curious how 
you can tell the difference.

08:32.720 --> 08:35.570
You're not just making stuff up, right?

08:35.880 --> 08:38.980
W-Well, mostly from their positions, I guess?

08:38.980 --> 08:43.260
I guess no matter how pretty something is, 
you can get bored of staring at it, huh?

08:43.260 --> 08:44.490
Already?!

08:44.490 --> 08:47.340
You'll have to forgive 
my bonehead of a sister.

08:47.340 --> 08:50.090
I-I do think they're pretty, though!

08:52.930 --> 08:55.340
I expected this kind of response...

08:55.340 --> 08:58.600
<b>Happy Fireworks</b>

08:55.340 --> 08:58.600
<b>Happy Fireworks</b>

08:56.460 --> 08:58.600
So I made sure to bring these along.

08:59.420 --> 09:00.510
Fireworks!

09:00.510 --> 09:02.280
I want in on this!

09:02.280 --> 09:04.130
Better get some water ready!

09:06.880 --> 09:09.320
Sorry to interrupt your explanation.

09:09.320 --> 09:11.430
I'm just glad everyone's excited.

09:12.060 --> 09:16.390
The stars really are 
gorgeous up here, though.

09:16.390 --> 09:17.800
They are.

09:18.390 --> 09:20.400
Should I bring you some coffee?

09:20.400 --> 09:21.580
Good idea.

09:23.140 --> 09:25.560
I'll take one, too.

09:26.440 --> 09:28.530
You're not interested in the fireworks?

09:29.300 --> 09:32.160
Did you really think that childish 
distraction would work on me?

09:32.160 --> 09:35.990
I'll grab coffee for you all, then.

09:35.990 --> 09:36.840
You sure?

09:37.280 --> 09:40.970
Sure! It's your wedding reception, after all!

09:41.510 --> 09:45.510
How about you come help me, Chi-chan?

09:45.510 --> 09:47.120
Why should I?!

09:47.120 --> 09:49.120
And since when am I Chi-chan?!

09:50.650 --> 09:53.760
Thank you so much for everything 
today, Kaname-chan.

09:53.760 --> 09:57.190
Don't mention it! I'm just glad you're happy.

09:57.190 --> 09:59.950
It's great we were all able 
to celebrate like this.

09:59.950 --> 10:01.120
Hang on a minute.

10:01.990 --> 10:04.630
I'm not celebrating at all.

10:05.640 --> 10:09.500
I-It's been a while since we've 
talked, huh, Chitose-chan?

10:10.300 --> 10:13.780
We met in Kyoto, and since then, 
I think only at the takoyaki party?

10:14.560 --> 10:19.010
We barely talked on either 
of those occasions, either.

10:20.580 --> 10:22.760
Give him a break already.

10:23.040 --> 10:28.130
Something you said back then has 
really stuck with me, though.

10:29.650 --> 10:32.360
When you asked why we got married.

10:33.980 --> 10:35.330
I'm pretty sure marriage...

10:36.040 --> 10:39.050
most likely predates the 
invention of written language.

10:39.050 --> 10:43.580
Which would mean that it already existed 
the moment history was first recorded.

10:44.040 --> 10:48.800
I mean, I got married because 
I love Tsukasa-chan...

10:49.890 --> 10:54.710
But I do wonder why falling in love with 
someone makes you want to get married.

10:57.280 --> 10:58.920
I see.

10:58.920 --> 11:02.090
You've got quite the romantic 
head on your shoulders.

11:02.090 --> 11:03.490
Tokiko-san.

11:03.490 --> 11:05.880
Mind if I join you?

11:05.880 --> 11:07.380
Not at all.

11:07.380 --> 11:10.890
This place is absolutely gorgeous, by the way.

11:10.890 --> 11:13.310
Yes, it certainly is.

11:13.620 --> 11:16.360
Your explanation before 
was wonderful, as well.

11:16.360 --> 11:18.120
Such a clever boy.

11:18.120 --> 11:20.060
Aw, it's just a hobby of mine.

11:20.060 --> 11:24.790
Since your wife is more interested 
in the fireworks than the stars...

11:24.790 --> 11:28.270
Why don't we have a chat
about the stars over there?

11:28.270 --> 11:29.580
That sounds good!

11:29.580 --> 11:32.580
Now, hang on! What exactly is this?!

11:32.870 --> 11:37.090
Quit worrying. I just want 
to have a chat with Nasa-kun.

11:37.380 --> 11:42.470
Is that right? Well, it had 
better not be anything weird.

11:42.770 --> 11:46.160
Oh, come on. Everything I say 
is weird, and you know it.

11:46.160 --> 11:48.100
Now, let's be on our way, Nasa-kun.

11:48.100 --> 11:49.560
Oh, sure.

11:49.560 --> 11:51.100
Hey!

11:51.420 --> 11:53.980
In that case, don't take him!

11:54.310 --> 11:55.120
Come on!

11:55.120 --> 11:57.030
Are you listening?!

12:00.500 --> 12:03.610
So, how is newlywed life treating you?

12:03.930 --> 12:05.680
Let's see...

12:05.680 --> 12:08.050
Well, every day has something new.

12:08.050 --> 12:10.710
I'm learning and discovering so much,

12:10.710 --> 12:12.120
which makes it a lot of fun.

12:12.360 --> 12:13.620
I see.

12:14.090 --> 12:16.130
I'm glad to hear that.

12:16.420 --> 12:20.000
I actually owe you a bit 
of an apology, Nasa-kun.

12:20.000 --> 12:21.630
What for?

12:21.940 --> 12:26.650
It's my fault that it took two 
years for you two to be reunited.

12:26.650 --> 12:30.520
She indulged a selfish request 
of mine for two whole years.

12:31.630 --> 12:36.020
Which is why I'm really grateful that 
you waited for her for so long.

12:36.660 --> 12:40.860
Nasa-kun, do you remember 
the night you met her?

12:40.860 --> 12:46.210
To be honest, right after she told me 
she'd go out with me if we got married,

12:46.210 --> 12:47.530
I lost consciousness.

12:47.990 --> 12:51.950
So I don't really know how 
I ended up in the hospital.

12:52.660 --> 12:56.110
I see. In that case, you still must not—

12:56.110 --> 12:56.560
But...

12:57.310 --> 12:59.560
I'm not that dense.

12:59.560 --> 13:01.550
I think I have a hunch as to what's going on.

13:02.960 --> 13:06.300
And... even when you account for that,

13:07.490 --> 13:13.310
I'm really glad to be 
married to Tsukasa-chan.

13:13.600 --> 13:17.940
<i>Oh, I see. Then it really is true.</i>

13:17.940 --> 13:22.440
<i>He's the one to finally 
make your wish come true.</i>

13:23.480 --> 13:26.950
I'm glad. This is such a relief.

13:27.330 --> 13:31.800
You were talking before about 
why people get married, right?

13:31.800 --> 13:32.720
That's right.

13:33.180 --> 13:37.760
I asked her the same question once before.

13:37.760 --> 13:40.030
If you're curious, you should ask her.

13:40.030 --> 13:43.510
Make sure you're alone when 
you do. I'm sure she'll tell you.

13:44.110 --> 13:46.590
Okay, the old lady is done talking.

13:46.840 --> 13:48.030
Go on, now.

13:49.670 --> 13:50.750
And thank you.

13:51.350 --> 13:54.900
Take good care of her.

14:00.510 --> 14:02.610
<i>It was a moonlit night.</i>

14:11.850 --> 14:16.120
<i>I found myself rushing as 
I was searching for you.</i>

14:16.920 --> 14:20.630
<i>From the moment I first saw you,
 I thought it was destiny.</i>

14:41.420 --> 14:42.510
Tsukasa-chan.

14:43.150 --> 14:44.770
Oh, darling.

14:44.770 --> 14:46.780
What brings you out here?

14:47.060 --> 14:50.280
Oh, it's nothing important.

14:50.280 --> 14:53.890
I just noticed you can 
see Mount Fuji from here.

14:53.890 --> 14:55.290
Hey, you're right.

14:56.010 --> 14:58.000
Did you finish your talk with Tokiko?

14:58.000 --> 14:58.700
Yeah.

14:59.390 --> 15:01.880
Is everyone still playing with fireworks?

15:01.880 --> 15:04.690
Yep. I think the night is going 
to last quite a bit longer.

15:06.010 --> 15:10.640
Tokiko-san really cares about 
you, doesn't she, Tsukasa-chan?

15:10.640 --> 15:13.800
She's always been a little too attached.

15:15.220 --> 15:18.090
The way everyone showed up 
to celebrate our marriage...

15:18.870 --> 15:20.560
We need to pay them back someday.

15:21.680 --> 15:27.570
Well, I like the idea of us taking 
everyone on a surprise trip next time.

15:28.360 --> 15:30.390
So, what did Tokiko say?

15:30.390 --> 15:33.820
She asked what it was like 
being married to you.

15:35.070 --> 15:36.950
She didn't ask anything weird, did she?

15:36.950 --> 15:39.310
Nothing weird, no.

15:39.310 --> 15:46.560
But she said I should ask you about that 
"Why do people get married?" question.

15:46.560 --> 15:48.460
Of course she did.

15:51.780 --> 15:53.970
What do you think, Tsukasa-chan?

15:53.970 --> 15:55.220
Good question...

15:55.570 --> 15:58.720
I'm sure there are all sorts of reasons,

15:59.060 --> 16:04.320
but I think the big one is 
that no one lives forever.

16:07.280 --> 16:10.610
Don't worry, I'm not getting 
maudlin or anything.

16:11.610 --> 16:14.110
It's just something I've noticed over time...

16:14.700 --> 16:18.090
No matter what great things you achieve
 or how much wealth you acquire,

16:18.090 --> 16:20.120
even if your name goes down in history...

16:20.520 --> 16:23.700
One day, you'll suddenly be gone.

16:25.370 --> 16:27.630
It could be illness. Injury.

16:28.000 --> 16:29.380
Maybe a war.

16:29.730 --> 16:31.130
Might even be an accident.

16:31.450 --> 16:33.380
If you're lucky, you make 
it to around 100 years...

16:33.800 --> 16:35.890
But you'll get old, and then you'll be gone.

16:36.510 --> 16:38.890
You can't fight it, even if you want to.

16:38.890 --> 16:43.340
Everyone who is born reaches
 the end at some point.

16:44.920 --> 16:46.150
And that's exactly why...

16:46.650 --> 16:48.650
they want to believe.

16:50.690 --> 16:54.150
That if nothing else, 
their love will last forever.

16:56.260 --> 17:02.780
Even if their bodies fall apart, 
what they had will live on eternally.

17:09.770 --> 17:14.050
It could be as transient as falling 
snow that melts on the ground,

17:14.430 --> 17:16.800
or as faint as a whispered prayer.

17:16.800 --> 17:20.400
But still, people want a light 
that will never fully fade.

17:21.560 --> 17:25.440
That's why getting married 
involves promises, right?

17:25.690 --> 17:30.320
To your parents, your mentors, 
and the people who have faith in you.

17:30.830 --> 17:33.320
You make a vow on an unbreakable 
stone that represents eternity.

17:34.240 --> 17:35.070
And...

17:35.980 --> 17:39.550
You make it to what we call God, 
which may as well be the universe itself.

17:42.420 --> 17:44.950
In sickness and in health,

17:45.290 --> 17:47.710
in joy and in sorrow,

17:48.080 --> 17:50.710
for rich or for poor,

17:50.710 --> 17:53.210
you love and honor each other,

17:53.210 --> 17:55.720
consoling and aiding each other,

17:56.100 --> 17:59.720
dedicating yourselves for 
as long as you both live.

17:59.720 --> 18:02.850
Creating a love between the two of 
you that couldn't exist without both.

18:10.720 --> 18:12.130
It's a promise.

18:15.210 --> 18:17.210
<i>It was a moonlit night.</i>

18:20.520 --> 18:24.870
<i>We promised to love each other 
forever under this starry sky.</i>

18:27.470 --> 18:32.130
Wait, you mean <i>Draco Bol</i> doesn't 
end after he beats the Demon King?!

18:32.130 --> 18:35.590
That's right. Remember when he 
said it'd go on "a little bit longer"?

18:35.590 --> 18:38.240
They start fighting aliens 
and stuff afterwards,

18:38.240 --> 18:40.340
so it's more like that's 
where it really starts.

18:40.340 --> 18:42.760
Wow! Making manga must be hard!

18:42.760 --> 18:44.140
Seriously!

18:49.200 --> 18:50.240
And that being the case,

18:50.240 --> 18:55.780
we prepared a special glamping tent for you 
two that's a bit away from everyone else.

18:56.000 --> 18:59.490
That's what she said, but is this it?

18:59.490 --> 19:02.530
It is technically a tent.

19:07.280 --> 19:11.200
The roof on this thing is transparent. 
You can see the sky.

19:11.200 --> 19:13.040
Talk about romantic...

19:13.040 --> 19:14.790
Really.

19:14.790 --> 19:16.050
So I guess...

19:16.050 --> 19:18.550
this is where we sleep tonight.

19:19.360 --> 19:20.300
On a bed...

19:21.000 --> 19:23.320
That's one big bed, huh?

19:23.320 --> 19:26.810
S-Sure is. I guess it might be a king?

19:27.260 --> 19:30.280
There are cold drinks, too.

19:30.280 --> 19:34.140
W-Wow. We might as well help ourselves.

19:35.650 --> 19:40.390
Anyway, it really is a lovely view!

19:40.390 --> 19:41.820
It sure is.

19:44.760 --> 19:48.070
Hey! Is it okay if I get closer?!

19:48.070 --> 19:50.080
S-Sure! Go ahead.

19:54.960 --> 19:57.840
<i>He is a very smart boy.</i>

19:58.260 --> 20:04.150
<i>Due to his hard-working nature, he also 
has an agile mind full of knowledge.</i>

20:04.150 --> 20:07.850
<i>And right now, his considerable intelligence
 was fully focused on one thing:</i>

20:09.000 --> 20:12.730
<i>How much can we fool around in here, anyway?</i>

20:12.730 --> 20:14.600
<i>What a waste of brainpower!</i>

20:15.090 --> 20:19.260
<i>I mean, since we're going to be 
sleeping in that big bed together,</i>

20:19.260 --> 20:22.360
<i>I would like to fool around 
as much as possible.</i>

20:23.260 --> 20:27.870
<i>But it kills me to admit we're inside a tent,
 which offers just about zero soundproofing.</i>

20:28.650 --> 20:33.170
<i>So if my wife starts making sweet sounds,</i>

20:33.580 --> 20:37.380
<i>everyone we know might be able to hear!</i>

20:38.080 --> 20:40.410
<i>Not that I mind, personally!</i>

20:41.620 --> 20:44.010
<i>But speaking from personal experience,</i>

20:44.010 --> 20:48.390
<i>since we haven't had a chance 
to shower and clean ourselves up,</i>

20:48.390 --> 20:51.740
<i>Tsukasa-chan might not want to be held at all.</i>

20:52.190 --> 20:53.640
<i>That being said...</i>

20:54.320 --> 20:57.730
<i>She's also cute when she's a little hesitant!</i>

20:57.730 --> 20:59.650
<i>He's just a perv at this point.</i>

21:03.280 --> 21:06.350
Darling, what's the hand for?

21:06.350 --> 21:07.850
Well, y'know...

21:07.850 --> 21:09.200
I wonder!

21:09.200 --> 21:10.350
<i>You do?</i>

21:12.660 --> 21:15.840
I was just thinking... 
the stars are really pretty.

21:15.840 --> 21:17.420
What does that have to do with it?

21:17.890 --> 21:18.920
B-But still!

21:19.280 --> 21:20.760
The stars might be pretty,

21:20.760 --> 21:23.500
but you're really pretty 
yourself, Tsukasa-chan!

21:24.140 --> 21:26.180
Th-Thank you?

21:26.400 --> 21:27.050
Yep.

21:29.960 --> 21:33.120
<i>Huh? How do I invite her to bed now?</i>

21:33.120 --> 21:35.690
<i>Seriously, what do normal couples do?</i>

21:36.280 --> 21:39.360
<i>Do they just go, "Let's move to the bed,"
 when the mood is like this?</i>

21:39.360 --> 21:41.690
<i>And wouldn't that be super embarrassing?!</i>

21:42.000 --> 21:44.680
<i>Not to mention it's so direct 
that it's a little scary!</i>

21:44.680 --> 21:48.320
<i>Shouldn't there be some sort of 
code word for adults that we can use?</i>

21:48.320 --> 21:51.850
<i>If there is, they should teach it at school!</i>

21:51.850 --> 21:53.210
<i>Wh-What do I do?</i>

21:53.210 --> 21:57.690
<i>I mean, if possible, I'd like to fool 
around with my wife on this bed!</i>

22:00.060 --> 22:01.270
Tsukasa-chan...

22:01.270 --> 22:02.710
Y-Yeah?

22:03.750 --> 22:09.090
Would you like to look at the stars 
on the b-b-bed instead of over here?

22:10.910 --> 22:15.980
S-S-Sounds good. That might be 
a nice view of the stars, too.

22:15.980 --> 22:21.390
Th-Then I'll turn the lights down
 so we can have a better view.

22:21.390 --> 22:22.760
S-Sure.

22:31.600 --> 22:33.480
They really are pretty.

22:34.040 --> 22:36.250
We can see the moon, too.

22:36.530 --> 22:40.610
Um... d-do you want to 
put your head on my arm?

22:40.610 --> 22:45.510
I-I see. That's a nice idea, darling.

22:48.700 --> 22:51.500
Th-This sure is a fluffy bed.

22:51.970 --> 22:53.930
I-It is.

22:54.720 --> 22:56.940
I had a great time today.

22:57.760 --> 23:00.690
Y-Yeah. I did, too.

23:03.340 --> 23:07.690
<i>To be honest, I'm not really 
sure what to do from here.</i>

23:08.310 --> 23:09.700
Tsukasa-chan...

23:10.320 --> 23:11.850
You smell nice.

23:13.510 --> 23:16.990
B-But I sweated a lot today.

23:17.560 --> 23:20.690
It still smells really nice.

23:20.690 --> 23:22.680
That tickles!

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.720 --> 23:28.760
We were united and given the 
blessings of many people.

23:28.760 --> 23:30.610
I love my husband.

23:30.610 --> 23:32.510
I will make Tsukasa-chan happy.

23:32.910 --> 23:34.510
Fate was kind enough to bring us together,

23:34.850 --> 23:37.520
and now, for all the months 
and years that will follow...

23:37.520 --> 23:38.520
We'd like to say...

23:38.970 --> 23:40.020
Thank you.
